			:background "The series parodies many famous fairy tales, either with puns relating to names or fairy tale themes being used in creative and funny ways.  The two main heroines&#039; names are a play on words relating to the story of Little Red Riding Hood; Akai means red and Ookami means wolf.  The title of the anime is a pun for the full title of Snow White and translates to Wolf and the Seven Companions; additionally, Ringo means apple and Ryouko means hero, making their names double puns. Other fairy tale parodies include Cinderella and The Ant and the Grasshopper." ;
